.el .ds Aq '
.TH sam-jail 1 2026-11-10 "SAM 0.1.0" "SAM - Sandboxed AppImage Manager"
.SH NAME
sam\-jail \- SAM \- Sandboxed AppImage Manager: Flatseal\-style permission manager and sandbox launcher for AppImages
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBsam\-jail\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
SAM \- Sandboxed AppImage Manager: Flatseal\-style permission manager and sandbox launcher for AppImages
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print machine\-readable JSON
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
sam\-jail\-scan(1)
Find AppImages in the scan directories
.TP
sam\-jail\-discover(1)
List AppImages in the scan folders and menu, sandboxed or not. Reads names and icons without unpacking or running anything
.TP
sam\-jail\-add(1)
Create a sandbox for an AppImage: extract, profile, add a menu entry
.TP
sam\-jail\-preview(1)
Settings SAM would use for an AppImage without a sandbox (nothing is unpacked). With \-\-permissions\-stdin, evaluates adjusted settings
.TP
sam\-jail\-hints(1)
Things to check right after creating a sandbox, with one\-click fixes
.TP
sam\-jail\-repair(1)
Repair an app that does not start or misbehaves: list steps, apply one, or undo
.TP
sam\-jail\-selftest(1)
Start sandboxed apps briefly and report which ones keep running. Opens their windows for a few seconds
.TP
sam\-jail\-menu(1)
Show, hide or restore unsandboxed menu entries for a sandboxed app
.TP
sam\-jail\-list(1)
List registered apps
.TP
sam\-jail\-info(1)
Show details about an app
.TP
sam\-jail\-remove(1)
Remove an app, its extraction, launcher and (unless \-\-keep\-data) its private home. Refuses while the app runs, unless \-\-stop
.TP
sam\-jail\-stop(1)
Close a running app (it gets the chance to save and quit first)
.TP
sam\-jail\-uninstall(1)
Remove SAM from this computer: every sandbox (menu entries SAM hid come back), SAM\*(Aqs menu entries, its settings and the apps\*(Aq private data. AppImage files stay. Lists what it would remove without \-\-yes
.TP
sam\-jail\-run(1)
Run an app in its sandbox
.TP
sam\-jail\-command(1)
Show the generated sandbox command without running it
.TP
sam\-jail\-doctor(1)
Check the system (or one app) for problems
.TP
sam\-jail\-version(1)
Show the version and the level of the JSON interface
.TP
sam\-jail\-updates(1)
Check whether newer versions are published (one app, or all). Contacts the update source each AppImage names (GitHub or its own server); nothing is downloaded or replaced
.TP
sam\-jail\-update(1)
Download the newest published version of an app\*(Aqs AppImage and put it in place of the old one (kept, so `\-\-undo` can go back). Settings and files stay
.TP
sam\-jail\-self\-update(1)
Update SAM itself, when it runs from its AppImage ($APPIMAGE)
.TP
sam\-jail\-space(1)
Disk space of one app, or of every app
.TP
sam\-jail\-free\-space(1)
Delete an app\*(Aqs unpacked copy; the next start unpacks it again
.TP
sam\-jail\-logs(1)
Show logs for an app
.TP
sam\-jail\-preset(1)
Manage presets
.TP
sam\-jail\-set(1)
Set one permission, e.g. `sam\-jail set krita network.mode none`
.TP
sam\-jail\-get(1)
Read permissions (all, or one key)
.TP
sam\-jail\-profile(1)
Read or replace the full profile (JSON on stdin for `set`)
.TP
sam\-jail\-evaluate(1)
Risk and warnings for a permission set given as JSON on stdin
.TP
sam\-jail\-verify(1)
Check that the app\*(Aqs sandbox gives it exactly what its settings say: starts the sandbox with a probe instead of the app. Also takes an AppImage without a sandbox: then the settings it would get are checked (nothing is unpacked or stored)
.TP
sam\-jail\-compat(1)
Turn compatibility mode on or off. Off restores the settings from before it was turned on
.TP
sam\-jail\-args(1)
Show the extra arguments always passed to the app, or replace them with a JSON list on stdin (`\-\-stdin`)
.TP
sam\-jail\-review(1)
Mark an app\*(Aqs profile as reviewed
.TP
sam\-jail\-reextract(1)
Re\-extract the AppImage (after updates or failures)
.TP
sam\-jail\-redetect(1)
Re\-run dependency detection and the recommendation
.TP
sam\-jail\-refresh(1)
Check AppImages for changes (stale/missing)
.TP
sam\-jail\-relocate(1)
Point an app at the new location of its AppImage
.TP
sam\-jail\-desktop(1)
Install or remove the desktop launcher. `sam\-jail desktop all refresh` rewrites every launcher whose command is outdated (e.g. SAM\*(Aqs AppImage was moved)
.TP
sam\-jail\-diagnose(1)
Run the app once under strace to find missing resources
.TP
sam\-jail\-report(1)
Print a redacted bug report
.TP
sam\-jail\-config(1)
Read or change configuration
.TP
sam\-jail\-permissions(1)
List all permissions with plain\-language explanations
.TP
sam\-jail\-cleanup(1)
Remove extraction leftovers not referenced by any app
.TP
sam\-jail\-onboarding(1)
First\-run onboarding status
.TP
sam\-jail\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
.SH VERSION
v0.1.0
